abstract: "In the continuous-time model of cultural trait accumulation of Wakano, Ohtsuki, Kobayashi and Baake (2026), each trait is copied at an encounter with probability b and encounters occur 1/b times as often, so the per-trait transmission rate is fixed. The expected number of traits, and the expected number held by exactly k individuals, do not depend on b, but every such count increases in convex order with b: variance, expected shortfall below any target and the probability of an empty repertoire all rise with bundling. Strictness is characterised exactly; the ordering extends to bundled forgetting and, with Poisson innovation, to the discrete-generation Versions 2, 1 and 3 of Wakano and Aoki (2024). Above the critical learning rate the effect is large. Neutral model, no empirical data. Unrefereed candidate; internal AI-assisted review only. Text CC0-1.0; code MIT."
